# Three of these are REQUIRED in production and have no safe default there:
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and BETTER_AUTH_URL. With NODE_ENV=
# production a missing one throws at module load, so the deploy fails rather
# than the first user (ticket 112, src/lib/env.ts). Everything else below is
# genuinely optional and degrades — see CLAUDE.md rule 11.
#
# --- Database (ticket 02: Turso / libSQL + Drizzle) -------------------------
# Local dev works with no Turso account: a file-backed libSQL database.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL="file:./local.db"
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=""   # required only for a hosted Turso database

# --- Auth (tickets 03 / 06: Better Auth) ------------------------------------
# openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="dev-only-secret-change-me"
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Google OAuth is optional locally — omit both and only email/password shows.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# --- A local test account (#no-ticket) --------------------------------------
# Set both and `/api/dev/sign-in` starts answering: POST signs a browser in,
# GET hands the phone app the credentials for its "Sign in as the dev user"
# button. Either one missing, or NODE_ENV=production, and the route 404s.
# The account has to already exist — sign up once through the site.
# FLOC_DEV_USER_EMAIL=""
# FLOC_DEV_USER_PASSWORD=""

# --- Maps (v0.2 tickets 15/12: Nominatim geocoding + OpenStreetMap tiles) ---
# No key, no account, no variable. Both providers are free and identified by a
# hardcoded User-Agent (src/server/places.ts). Nominatim unreachable or rate-
# limited -> place pickers fall back to free-text place names.

# --- Email (ticket 08: Resend) ----------------------------------------------
# Omit and outbound email is logged to the server console instead of sent.
# RESEND_API_KEY=""
EMAIL_FROM="Floc <no-reply@floc.example>"

# --- Notifications (#345, #346) --------------------------------------------
# The Railway cron calls POST /api/cron/push with this as a Bearer token.
# Without it the route answers 404 to everyone, and nothing sends.
# CRON_SECRET=""
# Optional: only if "enhanced push security" is on at expo.dev.
# EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=""

# --- App links (#346) ------------------------------------------------------
# Let an emailed link open the phone app. Omit and /.well-known answers 404,
# so links simply open the website.
# SHA-256 of the Android signing certificate(s), comma-separated (Play Console
# → App integrity, or `eas credentials`).
# ANDROID_CERT_SHA256=""
# The Apple Developer team id.
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=""

# --- Documents (ticket 239: trip files) -------------------------------------
# Where uploaded bookings/tickets are written. On Railway this is a mounted
# volume's path. Omit it and the whole Documents feature hides — no block on
# Overview, no upload (rule 11). Nothing else in the app depends on it.
# FLOC_FILES_DIR="./.uploads"

# --- Billing (ticket 245: Stripe, test mode) --------------------------------
# Omit every variable below and Pro simply never sells: the gate reads the
# local subscription table, which stays empty, so nothing crashes and every
# Pro surface shows its lock (rule 11). Wiring lands in ticket 246.
#
# Test keys everywhere, production included, until the legal pages exist
# (ticket 249). Test keys start `sk_test_` / `pk_test_` and move no money.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
#
# From the webhook endpoint in the Stripe dashboard. Without it the webhook
# route rejects every call, because an unverified webhook lets anyone POST
# themselves a subscription.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
#
# Price IDs (`price_...`), not amounts. Stripe owns the £3.99/£29.99; the app
# only ever names them, so a price change is a dashboard edit, not a deploy.
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=""
# STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY=""

# --- Billing in the phone app (Apple and Google) -----------------------------
# Omit these and the app's store purchases are refused as "unavailable" —
# nothing is recorded, nothing crashes (rule 11). Products are named in
# @floc/core/billing/store-products, not here.
#
# Apple: the bundle id, the numeric Apple ID from App Store Connect, and Apple's
# root certificates (https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/ — Apple Root
# CA G3), each DER file base64-encoded, comma-separated. Both production and
# sandbox receipts are accepted, because App Review buys in the sandbox.
# App Store Server Notifications V2 URL: <site>/api/billing/app-store
# APPLE_BUNDLE_ID="com.floc.app"
# APPLE_APP_ID=""
# APPLE_ROOT_CERTS=""
#
# Google: the package name and a service account JSON (the whole key file, one
# line) with "View financial data" on the app in Play Console.
# GOOGLE_PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME="com.floc.app"
# GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=""
#
# Real-time developer notifications: a Pub/Sub push subscription to
# <site>/api/billing/play with authentication on. The audience you set there,
# and the push service account's email. Without both, every push is refused.
# GOOGLE_PLAY_RTDN_AUDIENCE=""
# GOOGLE_PLAY_RTDN_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=""

# --- The paid tier, switched off ------------------------------------------
#
# "true" hands every gated feature to everybody and hides every Pro surface:
# the landing block, the Billing panel and the gold badge. Set it while Pro
# is not ready to sell — the gates otherwise take the weather forecast and
# the packing auto-fill away from every user on the day they ship.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALL_FEATURES_FREE="true"
